WEBVTT

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.140
Organ and Limb Modification,
compiled by Burando Ayame.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:29.610
This text is a record of our time
with the one they call immortal.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.690
I, Burando Ayame,

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:36.370
for the betterment of medical science,
will bear this great responsibility and make

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.620
detailed records of the proceedings.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.680
Blade of the Immortal

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.050
One two three

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.220
Undead tree

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.640
What truth

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.560
I'll come true

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.900
Wow

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.700
I see that bright light

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:26.000
This is all I have

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.500
What did you say?
I know

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.050
Why do you say?

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.640
Hone the blade
Lie around

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.930
Survive of vision

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.060
Death and pleasure are my future

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:51.770
I got lost
I was lost

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:55.440
Survive of vision

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.780
Unfinished heaven

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.580
Now fight to claim your wounds

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.460
Don't know why
Don't know why

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:11.170
Survive of vision

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.690
I've brought the object of the research.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.690
You! Habaki!

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.530
My first impression of the immortal man
is that he was barbaric.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:57.210
There are two main tasks assigned to me
by the Shogunate official, Mr. Habaki.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:02.680
One, to modify the organs and bones
of the immortal man.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.140
Two, give a body properties similar to his.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.690
In other words, create another immortal.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:16.730
So, Mr. Habaki. How much time will I have
to bear fruit from these experiments?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:17.690
Eight days.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.860
What? Just eight days?

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:26.740
If eight days have passed with no results,
I will bring in someone else.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:31.370
But I have yet to even confirm
that he's truly immortal. You're telling me--

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.170
I've already examined him.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.420
It means nothing if I haven't seen it myself.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.380
Very well.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.870
Impossible!

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.620
He's in your hands now.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.640
We're sorry! We'll leave immediately!

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.720
Doa!

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.900
Hey, that hurt!

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.570
I'm sorry, but you went too far right there.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.610
Nothing's changed if you're like this.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.450
We're sorry.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:57.630
I swear to God,
she didn't mean to cause you any harm.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:00.000
It's just force of habit.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.010
Hang on.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:05.630
So, we're begging you.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.260
For what?

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.560
For lodging for a night.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.390
For someone who'd attack on first sight?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.850
Sorry. I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.820
So.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:25.200
The truth is, starting today, we're homeless.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:30.410
We'll find a place to live before tomorrow ends,
so please.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.830
Well, you see.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.800
To tell the truth, I really thought you'd give up
when you realized the place wasn't vacant.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.920
I knew killing her would have been quicker.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.760
I could tell you weren't here to rob the place
after talking to you, but...

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:55.060
I don't really mind if you stay a while.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:57.940
However...

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.070
Don't blame me for whoever shows up
or whatever happens.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:06.570
This place has a long history of happenings.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.100
What?

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:39.730
What are you doing?

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:41.610
Tobacco.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.070
Give me some spinach.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:59.620
Doa is how I'll refer to you. Let me ask you directly,

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.590
could you explain to me what exactly your intent was
with the training room wall?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.590
A window.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.680
There's already a lattice window.
From one end to the other.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:16.010
The good spirits can't move freely
through a tiny window like that.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:19.020
Bad spirits. Good spirits.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:23.610
You need a window that will let your offerings
to the spirits get through.

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:26.480
Every house in my village had one.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:30.700
Lots of bad stuff happened here in the past, right?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:35.240
I'm sure the house's bad construction
caused bad spirits to gather.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.370
I'm sorry.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.790
Well, I'm going out for a bit.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.880
Right, I'll have something figured out here
by the time you're back.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.260
Have Doa help you too.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:54.720
Right. What? That might be difficult.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.720
You must have her help you!

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.930
Right.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.310
How annoying. Just die.

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:03.980
HABAKI

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.200
Miss Hyakurin.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:23.960
Oh, look, it's Rin. What are you doing here?

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:27.750
I have a favor to ask.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:34.300
Like I said, Mr. Manji returned home some time ago.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:39.600
Then allow me to go up there. Otherwise,
call your boss. I won't take much of his time.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.810
My lord is currently in attendance at the castle,
and will not return until the evening.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.690
Is that so? Then I'll see you again tonight.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:52.240
Though, he did instruct me to give you this
if you happened to stop by.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.320
Second seat of the Mugai-ryu, Giichi.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.870
Third seat of the Mugai-ryu, Hyakurin.
The two aforementioned

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:05.040
are relieved of their positions on the day
this notice is read,

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:09.800
and furthermore on that same day,
the Mugai-ryu is forever disbanded.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.630
Signed, former Mugai-ryu commander,
Kagimura Habaki.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.180
He fired you?

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:28.360
Rin, Mr. Manji might be caught up
in something rather troublesome.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:30.520
What do you mean troublesome?

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:35.400
I don't know. That's why I'm going
to seek out someone who might.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.700
It's Giichi.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:51.340
The blood drawn shows no irregularities.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.800
No visible difference from the normal blood.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:58.550
I've confirmed with Manji that his head and heart
can both heal as well.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:04.180
However, studying just the surface will only yield
that he is normal.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.230
You figure something out?

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.820
Today's proceedings have come to a close.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:19.360
Where in the world did Mr. Manji and Mr. Giichi go?

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:25.370
Welcome back!

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:30.500
I'm simmering rice and cooking fish right now.
Why don't you eat with us?

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:31.960
Wow, thank you!

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.520
By the way, how's the training room wall?

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.190
It's still...

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:05.620
There's no way this is one
of your village customs too. Tell me it's not.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.960
What was that? Are you a thief or something?

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:16.130
You look like you've killed tons of people.

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:21.340
It's nothing like that. I was a looter of little things.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:25.310
I was forced out of Edo, then turned around
and did the same thing once I got back.

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.390
So here I am.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:36.230
You may have been better off
just accepting a death penalty.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:40.240
Well, about that. You know Lord Habaki?

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:45.780
He said to me "we'll be using you in an experiment
to create an immortal body.

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:49.500
If we succeed, you're free to go.
If we fail, you will die.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:53.210
Any words you'd like to leave behind
in the event that you die?"

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:57.420
He didn't go into much detail,
but it's never too much

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.420
to talk about yourself and more if it's free.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:03.050
I've got a wife who's slow in the head
waiting for me at home.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:06.390
I was never able to send her enough money
to support her.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:11.520
So I told them to return me back to her
when they make my body durable.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:15.020
And you believed their lip service?

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.980
That's right. I believe them.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:24.740
All I can do is believe.
Well, it probably won't happen for me.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:28.200
Even if it works, the only life I can think to live
is a dishonest one.

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:34.210
I'm sure it would work on my wife.
Her heart is on the straight and narrow.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:40.630
What am I saying? A straight and narrow heart's
got nothing to do with it.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.680
Excuse me.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:50.180
This...

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:54.060
Yeah, it's fine. I've gotten used to it.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.730
I don't mind a little liveliness.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.820
Have you lived here since you were a child, Miss Rin?

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.110
Yes.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.910
Where are your parents?

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:10.330
They were killed.

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:11.660
Killed?

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:17.920
The killers were called the Itto-ryu.
Have you heard of them?

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.590
What did you just...?

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:31.470
Day three. I will perform something unheard of
even in the barbarian lands.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:34.180
A full-body anesthesia dissection.

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:38.440
A decision only made due to the fact he is immortal.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:44.240
Imagine that. You really can
force a person to fall asleep.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:48.570
This is my first time using it in an experiment too.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:50.620
It's almost like he's dead.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:54.080
Don't go putting jinxes on it now, Mr. Karukozawa.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:02.090
Mr. Burando. Have you done similar procedures
in other countries?

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:07.130
Certain theories claim that the organs of an otter
are very similar to a human's.

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.390
You don't mean...?

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:17.140
It's a joke. Rest assured, I, Burando Ayame,

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:22.320
from whites, to blacks, infants and elders,
and both virgins and whores,

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.900
have cut open 39 different people in total.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.860
Though they were all corpses.

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:50.590
Look at this! The wound isn't closing.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:56.140
It's as I thought, his ability to regenerate
and return to normal has gone dormant as well.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.180
-This means--
-Mr. Burando!

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:06.400
Wait! Just for a moment! I want to see inside!

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.530
Mr. Burando!

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:11.700
Mr. Karukozawa!

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:39.180
How goes the progress?

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:44.560
Sir, yesterday's failure
has given me something of a hint.

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:49.780
Therefore I have a great favor to ask of you.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:58.620
Mister, are you sure
you should be relaxing right now?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.080
I'm thinking about a prison break.

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.580
Setting aside myself,

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:07.250
taking an extended stay here
won't do you any good.

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:09.550
Yeah.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:19.970
I can't just leave you in here.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:23.060
Did you say something just now, Mister?

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:24.690
It's nothing.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.860
Have you got a headache?

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:31.240
My head and everything else.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:34.070
Is it that bad?

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:37.870
No, it's my side.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:40.870
What's all the fuss?

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:42.410
-Hey, Mister!
-Hey!

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.250
What in the world is this?

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:53.090
Hey, what is it?

00:16:54.510 --> 00:17:00.430
It's nothing. Just some food poisoning.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.440
Dewanosuke.

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:09.610
It seems the sun has finally begun to shine
in this cell.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:15.280
Miss Hyakurin. You said you found Mr. Giichi?

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.320
Yeah, but he was being quite the coward.

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.160
So I hit him with his sake bottle
and sobered him up.

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:22.700
Sake bottle?

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.380
He says he wants to speak with you.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:41.810
My stomach!

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.850
What? Again, Mister?

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:51.190
That's gross. Hey sir, can you take a look at him?

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.860
He's been like this since breakfast.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.410
Do you remember what the menu was?

00:17:57.490 --> 00:18:01.580
Tofu, rhubarb, sliced herring and...

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.920
You forgot something, doctor.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:14.590
Hey, you! Release him, or else!

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:16.930
Easy now. Do you really want to test me?

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.100
It's no use, just put that thing down.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:31.060
Okay, Dewanosuke, pick it up.

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:31.980
Right.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:34.900
Dewanosuke!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.610
What are you doing?

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:40.410
So you came, captain.

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.280
Manji, you little...

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:48.040
Hold it, don't do anything fishy. Calmly disarm, now.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.630
Well, well.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:00.550
Damn it!

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.980
Burando, you said a corresponding limb would work?

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:13.400
Yes!

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.990
I can't, I can't just die
before I can become immortal!

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:28.250
What?

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:33.380
What... Is that mine?

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.130
Burando!

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:39.590
Right! Toraemon, bring that right hand here!

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:41.010
Yes sir!

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:46.850
It's starting to hurt even more, doctor!

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.270
Quit struggling! The nerves won't connect.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:52.560
And this?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.860
Bring me the styptic.

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:00.280
It hurts! It hurts!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.650
Stop crying, you fool.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.450
If you stay calm,
your arm will certainly return to normal.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.660
That's fast.

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.460
Come, Toraemon. And bring that right hand.

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:22.340
Kagimura Habaki, I never suspected
that your poor taste could go this far.

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:26.390
Just what do you think people are, huh?
You listening?

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:28.810
What?

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.310
-Toraemon.
-You! Habaki, I'll kill you!

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:37.230
Hold him down like so until the two open wounds
have met and begin to connect.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:41.780
How is he?

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.780
He's unconscious.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:47.410
He's almost out of energy, so we should get him
to a proper bed.

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:50.500
Karukozawa.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:51.450
Yes, sir.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:03.840
Mr. Habaki, I just realized this but,

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:08.810
from here on, the ability to dismember
their two bodies at the exact same point

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.770
will be of utmost importance.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:14.890
Could I request you proffer someone capable?

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:20.320
I see. It will be done. We will use Asaemon Yamada.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:23.360
You mean Asa the beheader?

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:32.290
Open up!

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:38.380
I told you, you don't have to feed me.
The hand feels fine now.

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:41.170
No one's going to punish you for it.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:45.550
Oh, Mister...

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:47.760
How is your arm?

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.300
As you can see.

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:54.930
Pardon me, I'll be going.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:22:00.480
The stitching of the nerves went extremely well.

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:40.290
The Killer of 100 got brought in by Lord Habaki.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:47.800
If not for Lord Habaki's blessing, a deviant like you...

00:23:50.840 --> 00:23:52.720
Act Fourteen – Amendments
